                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brizomancy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44f8c745-fd45-3b6f-b0b2-91dd2741fdde",
                                        "entry_id": "271004b0-ba64-3561-8138-71abbb988302",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of Ancient Greek divination by the interpretation of dreams with the aid of the goddess Brizo; hence, divination by dreams."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f0f0a8d-3e03-418f-baf0-75d44d94c2aa",
                                                "sense_id": "44f8c745-fd45-3b6f-b0b2-91dd2741fdde",
                                                "text": "Scaramouch took himself off and applied to all sorts of Divination for the purpose of discovering where the lost bottle was lying. He tried [...] Brizomancy, or by the nodding sleep[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba4e6b5a-e019-4a93-a3ba-5ceaa908a60d",
                                                "sense_id": "44f8c745-fd45-3b6f-b0b2-91dd2741fdde",
                                                "text": "The very fact that each specific method, or variant, had a name, testifies to the prevalence and widespread recognition of divinatory practices. The prophetic inspiration of Brizo, a goddess of sleep, gave rise to brizomancy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85e7d0e6-8205-458c-b97f-c7d48ffe4c2c",
                                                "sense_id": "44f8c745-fd45-3b6f-b0b2-91dd2741fdde",
                                                "text": "A common name for succubus was Brizo, after the Greek Goddess of sleep whose title came from brizein, to enchant, and referred to a special kind of incubation known as brizomancy. Like the Babylonian dream-Goddess, Nanshe, Brizo brought prophetic dreams which were later called wet dreams."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
